{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg5sdvcqAfkJJiQoASZA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Approach.** [Co(ox)₃]³⁻ is low-spin d⁶, so the two bands are ¹A₁g→¹T₁g and ¹A₁g→¹T₂g. I used the strong-field expressions with configuration interaction (Δ = 10Dq). I wrote these from memory and did not check them against the full Tanabe–Sugano matrices, so treat the numbers as approximate.\n\n- E(¹T₁) = Δ − C − 86B²/Δ\n- E(¹T₂) = Δ + 16B − C − 90B²/Δ\n\n**Solution.**\n\n1. Subtracting the two equations gives E(¹T₂) − E(¹T₁) = 16B − 4B²/Δ = 6918 cm⁻¹.\n2. Neglecting the small second term gives B ≈ 432 cm⁻¹. Including it raises this slightly.\n3. Set C = 4.5B and solve the two equations iteratively. This converges to B ≈ 435 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 1957 cm⁻¹.\n4. Substituting back into the ¹T₁ equation gives Δ − 1957 − 86B²/Δ = 16 611. The configuration-interaction term 86B²/Δ is about 840 cm⁻¹, so Δ ≈ 19 400 cm⁻¹.\n5. Dq = Δ/10 ≈ 1940 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 1.94 × 10³ cm⁻¹, B ≈ 435 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 1957 cm⁻¹. This gives Δ ≈ 19 400 cm⁻¹ and B/B_free-ion ≈ 0.4, which is typical for Co(III).\n\n{\"Dq\": 1941, \"B\": 435, \"C\": 1957, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Low-spin d6 strong-field Tanabe-Sugano expressions for 1T1 and 1T2 with C/B = 4.5 give Dq and B.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1673,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f5daad4-8194-49cc-8f5d-1d3bad46c2c4","uuid":"213c23dd-2e93-436c-9348-683e7dfd6f8f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:37:23.279Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg5sdVotigSRUN6m5GHd"}
